  "prompt": "A 6-site spin-1/2 ring is governed by the periodic transverse-field Ising Hamiltonian H = -J * sum_{i=0}^{5} sigma^z_i sigma^z_{(i+1) mod 6} - h * sum_{i=0}^{5} sigma^x_i, with J = 1 and periodic boundary conditions (site 5 couples back to site 0). Sweep h/J from 0.10 to 3.00 in steps of 0.05 (39 parameter points). At each h, prepare the ground state and measure: (1) the squared order parameter M2 = <((1/6) sum_i sigma^z_i)^2>, (2) the Binder cumulant U4 = 1 - <m_z^4>/(3<m_z^2>^2), (3) the magnetic susceptibility chi = 6*(<m_z^2> - <|m_z|>^2), and (4) the bipartite von Neumann entanglement entropy S_A = -Tr[rho_A ln rho_A] for the 3-site half-chain subsystem A = {sites 0,1,2}, obtained by tracing out sites {3,4,5}. Use the Binder cumulant and susceptibility peak to identify the pseudo-critical field h_c. Use N_shots = 4096 per observable per parameter point. The periodic boundary conditions impose additional symmetry constraints on the quantum circuit; account for them in your state preparation. Compare the entanglement entropy profile across the sweep with the known logarithmic divergence near the critical point. Report: estimated_critical_point, critical_point_error (vs. reference 1.0), observable_accuracy (mean absolute deviation of all four observables from exact diagonalization), phase_classification_accuracy, and noise_aware_performance (standard deviation of h_c across 5 independent shot-noise runs at N_shots = 4096).\n\nTask inputs:\n{\n  \"physical_system\": \"1D transverse-field Ising model (TFIM), 6 sites, periodic boundary conditions\",\n  \"num_spins\": 6,\n  \"hamiltonian\": {\n    \"expression\": \"H = -J * sum_{i=0}^{5} sigma^z_i sigma^z_{(i+1) mod 6} - h * sum_{i=0}^{5} sigma^x_i\",\n    \"parameters\": {\n      \"J\": 1.0,\n      \"h\": \"swept\"\n    },\n    \"boundary_conditions\": \"periodic (ring geometry)\",\n    \"matrix_dimension\": 64,\n    \"symmetries\": \"Z2 symmetry (global spin flip), translation symmetry\"\n  },\n  \"parameter_sweep\": {\n    \"parameter\": \"h/J\",\n    \"values\": \"0.10, 0.15, 0.20, ..., 3.00\",\n    \"num_points\": 39,\n    \"step\": 0.05\n  },\n  \"observables_provided\": [\n    \"squared order parameter: M2 = <( (1/6) sum_i sigma^z_i )^2>\",\n    \"Binder cumulant: U4 = 1 - <m_z^4> / (3 * <m_z^2>^2) where m_z = (1/6) sum_i sigma^z_i\",\n    \"magnetic susceptibility: chi = N * (<m_z^2> - <|m_z|>^2)\",\n    \"bipartite von Neumann entanglement entropy: S_A = -Tr[rho_A log rho_A] for half-chain partition A = {sites 0,1,2}\"\n  ]\n}\n\nRequired Python interface:\ndef solve_tfim_6site_pbc():\nReturn a dictionary with these outputs: estimated_critical_point, critical_point_error, observable_accuracy, phase_classification_accuracy, noise_aware_performance\nSupported environment: Python 3.12; Qiskit 1.4.5, qiskit-aer 0.17.2, qiskit-algorithms 0.3.1, qiskit-optimization 0.6.1, PennyLane 0.45.1, NumPy, SciPy, NetworkX, dimod and neal (dwave-neal). Use qiskit_aer for Aer, qiskit_algorithms for algorithms, and QuantumCircuit.assign_parameters for parameter binding. qiskit.Aer, BasicAer, execute, aqua, and bind_parameters are unavailable. \nInclude imports and helper functions. Do not execute at import time. Put scientific explanations in code comments/docstrings. Return only Python code.",
